// Function-body non-deterministic MODIFIERS (`fn f() forall { … }`) inside spec
// functions. A modifier records its kind on the function's body block, lowered
// by a different codegen path (`visit_function_definition_body`) than an inline
// block. In proof mode every spec-function body is lowered, and the two kinds
// here lower differently: a `forall` body keeps its 0xfc wrapper and draw,
// while an `exists` body is reachability-lowered — vanilla WASM, its `@`
// hoisted into a hidden trailing choice parameter, its obligation carried as
// an exists-kind `inference.hspecs` entry. This is the spec-wrapped,
// analysis-legal counterpart of the negative fixture
// `nondet_body_modifiers.inf`; the `assume` body modifier, which stays a
// P001 rejection, lives in `spec_assume_body_modifier.inf`.
spec NondetBodyModifiers {
  fn forall_fn() forall {
    let x: i32 = @;
    assert(x == x);
  }
  fn exists_fn() exists {
    let y: i32 = @;
    assert(y == y);
  }
}
